## Authentication & Authorization

### Authentication Requirements

**MUST:**
- Use industry-standard protocols (OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, SAML)
- Implement token expiration (access tokens: 15-60 min, refresh tokens: hours/days)
- Store tokens securely (httpOnly cookies or secure storage)
- Implement token refresh before expiration
- Use strong password requirements (or better: SSO/passwordless)

**MUST NOT:**
- Store passwords in plain text
- Use weak hashing (MD5, SHA1)
- Implement custom crypto (use vetted libraries)
- Send tokens in URL parameters

### Authorization Requirements

**Principle of Least Privilege:**
- Users/services get minimum permissions needed
- Default deny (explicit allow required)
- Separate read and write permissions
- Role-based access control (RBAC) for PHI/PII

**Example:**
```typescript
// ✅ Explicit permission checks
async function getPrescription(prescriptionId: string, userId: string) {
  const prescription = await db.prescriptions.findById(prescriptionId);
  
  // Check: user has permission to view this prescription
  if (!canAccess(userId, prescription.patient_id, 'prescriptions:read')) {
    throw new ForbiddenError('Insufficient permissions');
  }
  
  return prescription;
}
```

