## Encryption Requirements

### Data at Rest

**MUST encrypt:**
- PII fields in databases
- PHI fields in databases
- Backups containing PII/PHI
- File storage containing PII/PHI

**Standards:**
- AES-256-GCM or better
- Key management via KMS (AWS KMS, Azure Key Vault, Google Cloud KMS)
- Key rotation policy (annually or per-compliance)

### Data in Transit

**MUST:**
- Use TLS 1.3 (or TLS 1.2 minimum)
- Enforce HTTPS for all API endpoints
- Validate certificates
- Use secure WebSocket (wss://) for real-time connections

**MUST NOT:**
- Send PII/PHI over unencrypted connections
- Accept self-signed certificates in production
- Disable certificate validation

