## Error Handling & Information Disclosure

### Error Messages

**MUST:**
- Return generic error messages to users
- Log detailed errors server-side
- Use error tracking (Sentry, Rollbar)

**MUST NOT:**
- Expose stack traces to users
- Include PII/PHI in error messages
- Reveal database structure or internal paths
- Show detailed validation errors that leak system info

**Example:**
```typescript
// ✅ Safe error handling
try {
  await processPayment(userId, cardToken);
} catch (error) {
  // Log details server-side (no PII)
  logger.error('Payment processing failed', { 
    user_id: userId, 
    error: error.message 
  });
  
  // Return generic message to user
  throw new Error('Payment processing failed. Please try again.');
}

// ❌ Information disclosure
throw new Error(`Payment failed: ${error.stack} for user ${userEmail}`);
```

