## Retention & Deletion

### Data Retention Requirements

**MUST:**
- Define retention periods for each data classification
- Automatically delete data after retention period
- Document retention policy

**Example retention policy:**
- **PHI:** 7 years (or per-regulation)
- **PII:** Until user deletes account + 30 days
- **Audit logs:** 1 year minimum (2-7 years for regulated industries)
- **Session data:** 24 hours after logout

### User Data Deletion

**MUST:**
- Provide user data deletion capability (GDPR right to erasure)
- Delete all associated data (not just user record)
- Delete from backups (or mark for deletion on restore)
- Confirm deletion to user

**Example:**
```typescript
async function deleteUserData(userId: string) {
  // Delete user data across all systems
  await db.users.delete(userId);
  await db.userPreferences.delete({ user_id: userId });
  await db.userActivity.delete({ user_id: userId });
  await cache.delete(`user:${userId}`);
  await auditLog('user_deletion', { user_id: userId });
}
```

