## Common Vulnerability Prevention (OWASP Top 10)

### 1. Broken Access Control
✅ Validate permissions on every request  
✅ Default deny  
✅ Disable directory listing  
❌ Never trust client-side permission checks

### 2. Cryptographic Failures
✅ Encrypt PII/PHI at rest and in transit  
✅ Use TLS 1.3  
✅ Use strong algorithms (AES-256, RSA-4096)  
❌ Never implement custom crypto

### 3. Injection
✅ Use parameterized queries  
✅ Validate and sanitize input  
✅ Use ORM frameworks  
❌ Never build queries with string concatenation

### 4. Insecure Design
✅ Threat modeling before build  
✅ Security requirements in planning  
✅ Defense in depth  
❌ Never skip security review for PHI/PII features

### 5. Security Misconfiguration
✅ Disable unnecessary features  
✅ Remove default accounts  
✅ Security headers configured  
❌ Never expose debug endpoints in production

### 6. Vulnerable Components
✅ Keep dependencies updated  
✅ Scan for vulnerabilities  
✅ Review security advisories  
❌ Never ignore critical vulnerabilities

### 7. Identification & Authentication Failures
✅ Multi-factor authentication  
✅ Strong password policy  
✅ Session timeout  
❌ Never store passwords in plain text

### 8. Software & Data Integrity Failures
✅ Code signing  
✅ Dependency integrity checks  
✅ CI/CD pipeline security  
❌ Never trust unsigned code

### 9. Security Logging & Monitoring Failures
✅ Log security events  
✅ Monitor for anomalies  
✅ Alert on suspicious activity  
❌ Never log PHI/PII in audit logs

### 10. Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)
✅ Validate URLs  
✅ Allowlist external services  
✅ Network segmentation  
❌ Never trust user-provided URLs without validation

